          "value": ""
        },
        {
          "alias": "description",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Loading JS from Block Components with dependency-aware ordering"
        },
        {
          "alias": "title",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Script Queue"
        },
        {
          "alias": "content",
          "culture": "en-US",
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "be80a795-b398-4baa-860a-ee68b7124f11",
                "key": "b1000002-3002-4000-a002-000000000002",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "alias": "richtext",
                    "culture": "en-US",
                    "editorAlias": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "value": {
                      "blocks": {
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": [],
                        "layout": {}
                      },
                      "markup": "\u003Ch2\u003EScript Queue \u2014 Loading JS from Block Components\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EThe Problem\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003EuTPro uses a \u003Cstrong\u003Edeferred loading strategy\u003C/strong\u003E \u2014 jQuery and plugins only load after user interaction (or 3s idle) to improve Core Web Vitals. This creates a challenge:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIf a block component renders its own \u003Ccode\u003E\u0026lt;script defer\u0026gt;\u003C/code\u003E tag, it may execute \u003Cstrong\u003Ebefore\u003C/strong\u003E jQuery is available \u2014 causing \u003Ccode\u003E$ is not defined\u003C/code\u003E errors.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode\u003ETimeline:\n\u251C\u2500 HTML parsed \u2192 component \u0026lt;script defer\u0026gt; executes immediately  \u274C jQuery not loaded yet\n\u251C\u2500 User interacts (or 3s idle)\n\u2514\u2500 jQuery \u002B plugins start loading\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EThe Solution: Script Queue\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003EComponents \u003Cstrong\u003Eregister\u003C/strong\u003E their JS file paths into a per-request queue. The Layout then renders them in the correct position \u2014 either inside the deferred loader (after jQuery) or as standalone \u003Ccode\u003E\u0026lt;script defer\u0026gt;\u003C/code\u003E tags.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode\u003EComponent.cshtml \u2192 Html.QueueScript() or Html.QueueStandaloneScript()\n                         \u2193\n              HttpContext.Items (per-request, dedup)\n                         \u2193\n_Layout.cshtml  \u2192 @Html.RenderScriptQueue()        \u2192 appends to deferred array\n                \u2192 @Html.RenderStandaloneScripts()   \u2192 renders \u0026lt;script defer\u0026gt; tags\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\u003Ch3\u003ETwo Methods\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Ctable\u003E\u003Cthead\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Cth\u003EMethod\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EUse when\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003EHow it loads\u003C/th\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/thead\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E\u003Ccode\u003EHtml.QueueScript(path)\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EScript \u003Cstrong\u003Eneeds jQuery\u003C/strong\u003E or other deferred libraries\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EAppended to sequential deferred loader (loads \u003Cstrong\u003Eafter\u003C/strong\u003E jQuery)\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E\u003Ccode\u003EHtml.QueueStandaloneScript(path)\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EScript is \u003Cstrong\u003Evanilla JS\u003C/strong\u003E, no dependencies\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ERendered as \u003Ccode\u003E\u0026lt;script defer\u0026gt;\u003C/code\u003E (loads independently, faster)\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/tbody\u003E\u003C/table\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBoth methods \u003Cstrong\u003Ededuplicate automatically\u003C/strong\u003E \u2014 same script registered twice = rendered once.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EUsage in Component\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode\u003E@if (Context.Request.IsBlockPreviewRequest())\n{\n    @* Preview mode: CSS only, no JS needed *@\n    \u0026lt;link rel=\u0022stylesheet\u0022 href=\u0022~/css/@CurrentSite.GetItem().Root.Name/Components/MyComponent.css\u0022 /\u0026gt;\n}\nelse\n{\n    @using (Html.SetSection(Model.GetType().ToString(), HtmlSectionBlockExtensions.Position.BodyBottom))\n    {\n        \u0026lt;link rel=\u0022stylesheet\u0022 href=\u0022~/css/@CurrentSite.GetItem().Root.Name/Components/MyComponent.css\u0022 /\u0026gt;\n    }\n\n    // QueueStandaloneScript: vanilla JS, no dependencies, loads via \u0026lt;script defer\u0026gt;\n    // QueueScript: needs jQuery, appended to deferred loader chain (loads AFTER jQuery)\n    Html.QueueStandaloneScript($\u0022/scripts/{CurrentSite.GetItem().Root.Name}/my-component.js\u0022);\n}\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EExample: Script that needs jQuery\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode\u003EHtml.QueueScript($\u0022/scripts/{CurrentSite.GetItem().Root.Name}/slider.js\u0022);\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\u003Ch4\u003EExample: Standalone script (no jQuery)\u003C/h4\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode\u003EHtml.QueueStandaloneScript($\u0022/scripts/{CurrentSite.GetItem().Root.Name}/cookie-consent-banner.js\u0022);\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EWhat Happens in the Layout\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cpre\u003E\u003Ccode\u003E\u0026lt;!-- Deferred loader: jQuery \u002B plugins \u002B QueueScript entries --\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;script\u0026gt;\n    (function(){\n        var scripts=[\n            \u0027/assets/scripts/jquery.min.js\u0027,\n            \u0027/assets/scripts/jquery.dropotron.min.js\u0027,\n            \u0027/scripts/uTPro/util.js\u0027,\n            \u0027/scripts/uTPro/main.js\u0027\n            ,\u0027/scripts/uTPro/slider.js\u0027        // from QueueScript\n        ];\n        // loads sequentially after user interaction or 3s idle\n    })();\n\u0026lt;/script\u0026gt;\n\n\u0026lt;!-- Standalone scripts: QueueStandaloneScript entries --\u0026gt;\n\u0026lt;script src=\u0022/scripts/uTPro/cookie-consent-banner.js\u0022 defer\u0026gt;\u0026lt;/script\u0026gt;\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/pre\u003E\u003Ch3\u003ERules\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Col\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EVanilla JS\u003C/strong\u003E (no dependencies) \u2192 \u003Ccode\u003EQueueStandaloneScript\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ENeeds jQuery\u003C/strong\u003E or any library in the deferred chain \u2192 \u003Ccode\u003EQueueScript\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ENever\u003C/strong\u003E put \u003Ccode\u003E\u0026lt;script src=\u0022...\u0022\u0026gt;\u003C/code\u003E directly in a component \u2014 use the queue\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ECSS\u003C/strong\u003E can still use \u003Ccode\u003ESetSection\u003C/code\u003E as before (no dependency ordering issues)\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EBoth methods are \u003Cstrong\u003Esafe to call multiple times\u003C/strong\u003E with the same path \u2014 dedup is automatic\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ol\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EArchitecture\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003EImplemented in \u003Ccode\u003EuTPro.Extension/ScriptQueueExtensions.cs\u003C/code\u003E:\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003EUses \u003Ccode\u003EHttpContext.Items\u003C/code\u003E for per-request storage (zero serialization cost)\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Ccode\u003EHashSet\u0026lt;string\u0026gt;\u003C/code\u003E for O(1) dedup\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EHTML-encodes paths to prevent XSS\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ETwo separate queues (deferred vs standalone) with independent storage keys\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Ctable\u003E\u003Cthead\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Cth\u003EFile\u003C/th\u003E\u003Cth\u003ERole\u003C/th\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/thead\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E\u003Ccode\u003EuTPro.Extension/ScriptQueueExtensions.cs\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EExtension methods (QueueScript, QueueStandaloneScript, RenderScriptQueue, RenderStandaloneScripts)\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E\u003Ccode\u003EViews/uTPro/_Layout.cshtml\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ECalls RenderScriptQueue() inside deferred array \u002B RenderStandaloneScripts() after\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E\u003Ccode\u003EViews/globalLayout.cshtml\u003C/code\u003E\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ECalls RenderStandaloneScripts() (no deferred loader in fallback layout)\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EComponent .cshtml files\u003C/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ECall Html.QueueScript() or Html.QueueStandaloneScript()\u003C/td\u003E\u003C/tr\u003E\u003C/tbody\u003E\u003C/table\u003E"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
